Doug's biblical priest execution -

Throw a rock and pace out how far you threw it.  Dig
out the walls of a shrine that has a priest you have
decided to kill.  Start at a square adjacent to the altar
but away from the missing wall, pace your count of
squares through the removed wall.  Mark the spot and
gather around 200 rocks and as many missiles as you
can find in the 3 squares parallel to the altar facing
the 3 rows the priest will move into.

Once you start throwing the priest will not be able to
reach you to fight you since priests don't leave their
altar.  If you paced back far enough the lightning bolt
the deity throws in anger after the priest dies will not
reach far enough to hit you.  If you run out of missiles
the 200 rocks will be more than enough to take out
the strongest priest.  Since priests heal you don't
want to run out before the priest dies, better to have
a hundred spare rocks after you finish than one arrow
not enough.

The result is an unprotected altar you can convert as
you wish.  In biblical quote of "let he who is without
sin cast the first stone" suggests that when you start
you really want your deity to not be angry with you,
your alignment to be positive and so on so the price of
killing the priest can be paid at the altar with sacrifices
and you convert it not it converts you.

The combination of pacing out your throwing range,
digging out the walls of the shrine, staying far enough away
that you don't get hit by the lightning bolt is why it is
not obvious.  The idea is old enough that it has been
discussed a bunch of times on RGRN but I think I was
the first to post it.



